From: HiKey960 kernel team <hikey960@example.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:42:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0009] drm/bridge: adv7533: fix DSI lane count register encoding

The ADV7533 register 0x1c (DSI lane control) uses bits [7:6] to encode
the number of DSI data lanes:
  00 = 1 lane, 01 = 2 lanes, 10 = 3 lanes, 11 = 4 lanes

The current code uses `dsi->lanes << 4`, which produces:
  1 lane  -> 0x10 (bits[7:6]=00) - accidentally correct for 1 lane
  2 lanes -> 0x20 (bits[7:6]=00) - WRONG, treated as 1 lane
  3 lanes -> 0x30 (bits[7:6]=00) - WRONG, treated as 1 lane
  4 lanes -> 0x40 (bits[7:6]=01) - WRONG, treated as 2 lanes

The correct formula is `(dsi->lanes - 1) << 6`:
  1 lane  -> 0x00 (bits[7:6]=00) - correct
  2 lanes -> 0x40 (bits[7:6]=01) - correct
  3 lanes -> 0x80 (bits[7:6]=10) - correct
  4 lanes -> 0xc0 (bits[7:6]=11) - correct

This bug causes the ADV7533 PLL to never lock when using more than
1 DSI data lane, resulting in no HDMI output signal.

Signed-off-by: HiKey960 kernel team <hikey960@example.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7533.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7533.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/adv7511/adv7533.c
@@ -68,7 +68,13 @@ void adv7533_dsi_power_on(struct adv7511 *adv)
 	struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi = adv->dsi;
 
-	/* set number of dsi lanes */
-	regmap_write(adv->regmap_cec, 0x1c, dsi->lanes << 4);
+	/*
+	 * Set number of DSI lanes. Register 0x1c bits [7:6]:
+	 *   00 = 1 lane, 01 = 2 lanes, 10 = 3 lanes, 11 = 4 lanes
+	 * The correct encoding is (lanes - 1) << 6, NOT lanes << 4.
+	 * lanes << 4 encodes 4 lanes as 0x40 which the chip reads as 2 lanes.
+	 */
+	regmap_write(adv->regmap_cec, 0x1c, (dsi->lanes - 1) << 6);
 
 	if (adv->use_timing_gen) {
